==English==

===Etymology===
{{back-form|grungy|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡɹʌndʒ/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ʌndʒ|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} [[dirt|Dirt]] or [[filth]], especially when difficult to [[clean]].
#: ''The cinema floor was covered in '''grunge''' deposited by the crowds.
# {{lb|en|informal}} The state of being [[filthy]]; [[grubbiness]].
#: ''Chad used to work as a coal miner, but couldn't handle the constant '''grunge'''.
# {{lb|en|music genre}} A [[subgenre]] of [[alternative rock]], originating from Seattle, Washington, which melds [[punk]] and [[metal]].
#: ''Alice liked to wear plaids and ripped jeans, and listen to '''grunge'''.

